Package: hd-bootloader-gfx
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: amd64
Maintainer: Erik Van Hamme <erik.vanhamme@gmail.com>
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Depends: python3, python3-pil, systemd-ukify, systemd-boot-efi, fontconfig, hd-base (>= 1.22), hd-desktop
Recommends: dkms
Provides: hd-bootloader
Conflicts: hd-bootloader
Replaces: hd-bootloader
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Description: HyprDebian minimalist EFI bootloader, graphical
 A small UEFI bootloader that shows a menu of the unified kernel images (UKIs)
 of the most recent kernels, each in a normal and a ZFS recovery profile, on
 the HyprDebian wallpaper of hd-desktop, in its JetBrains Mono Nerd Font.
 .
 hd-bootloader-update builds the UKIs and writes them, the bootloader and
 assets.efi to an EFI system partition. assets.efi holds the settings, the
 images, the menu and the DKMS MOK, which the bootloader hands to the kernel
 so that it loads the DKMS-built ZFS module under Secure Boot. The settings
 are the key hd-bootloader in /etc/hyprdebian/config.json. When the Secure
 Boot keys of hd-base are in /etc/hyprdebian/secboot, it signs the
 bootloader, assets.efi and the UKIs with the db key, using sbsign.
